acceptance_criteria: "Resolve lifecycle meaning through the SDK status registry, preserve immutable release attribution, and add non-git custom-registry regression evidence."
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T07:44:30.725Z",codex-agent,"Addressed with the shared chronological release ledger for PR #291: SDK status normalization and terminal_done registry roles determine publication ownership. CLI and host generation forward the tracker registry and preserve explicit status filters. Adversarial non-git fixtures include a custom done-role status named active_named_done, early active captures, edits and reopening; the owning frozen row remains stable across 500 catalog permutations."
  "2026-10-27T07:54:18.264Z",codex-agent,"Final regression evidence: test/release-ownership.test.ts passes 4 tests with zero failures/skips/cancels, including 500 catalog permutations, SDK status-role classification, actual host/standalone generation and explicit status filters without git. The linked test command passes. Shared generation/correction behavior is documented in docs/tracker-milestones.md and docs/release-corrections.md."
  "2026-10-27T08:01:34.045Z",codex-agent,"Implementation complete with focused and packed evidence linked on pmc-release-corrections and PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291. Final-head npm/Bun CI evidence is recorded in the PR after completion. Releasing the claim while retaining this item unclosed for orchestrator verification."
